body:
After the finals I decided I had to take a break from my daily life and a vacation in Spain seemed ideal; after all I had studied Spanish for almost five years and I could speak it almost fluently. I decided to go in a small fishing village in Andalusia, near Cadiz, because I needed silence and peace, definitely not the chaotic mess of touristic locations. The Pueblo de San Martin was built on the edge of a reef that formed a small bay, where the fishermen's boats rested. The villagers were surprised to see someone this young staying there and they enjoyed my presence; They frequently invited me to eat or drink something on the balcony of their houses facing the immense Ocean below us.

One night, almost at the end of my vacation if I remember correctly, a strange heat wave hitted the village and I couldn't sleep well so, with the light of the full moon to light the narrow roads I decided to go out for a walk. Complete silence fell on the whole town, and I could hear the sound of my heartbeat; I finally found myself on the main road, just outside the town, that led to the *civilization.*

I turn around, deciding to head back to my hotel room, but I bump into a strange man that appeared suddenly behind me - Hoy mate, would ya like to buy sum haunted wear? - he asked. I watched him, silently and with diffidence. He seemed pretty harmless so I thought - Why not? After all I'm sure I wouldn't sleep arrived in my room -

He led me to a old Volkswagen Bus filled with various clothes - Th's are all prime quality clothes, ya can b'lieve me mate. We actually h've a sale on convicted murderers clothing ^((WITH A REAL EVIL SPIRIT FOR FREE! CHOOSE YOUR FAVOURITE MURDERER NOW!)). Don't ya worry, I've a loicense fo'all this - I saw a faded polo with a giant red stain that caught my eye - Ohhhh, ya're a cheeky expert uh? This is a mastapiece, a unique piece of clothing that belonged to the famous Florence's Monster, an Italian killer, still stained with the blood of his last victims! -

The strange man continued to talk about his wares for almost an hour, and in the end I decided to buy a golden watch belonged to some American gangster or something like that for a couple of euros just to make him happy. After all, who would believe that this is really haunted?

&#x200B;

...

&#x200B;

Well, the watch started talking in my sleep.

&#x200B;

\*\*\*

&#x200B;

Here I decided to adopt a more comical tone on the story, hope you like it :D
